# privacy-allowlist — benign matches the privacy scan must ignore.
# Format: <file-glob><TAB><ERE>. The ERE is matched against the
# MATCHED TEXT of a hit (not the whole line), and the glob against the
# file path (shell-style: * matches any run of characters, ? one).
# A hit is dropped only when BOTH match. Everything else fails the scan.
# Every ERE is anchored (^...$): it must match the ENTIRE matched text.
# An unanchored entry would exempt longer values that merely contain it
# (2026-11-20 S24: an allowlisted address exempted a longer address
# sharing its prefix). The two reserved-domain
# entries use ^.+@...$ so a complete address at that domain is exempt,
# never a bare domain substring.
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Each entry names the audit finding that justifies it (2026-11-14
# published-set audit); do not add an entry without a reason.
#
# 10.0.2.2 — Android emulator host-loopback alias (audit b3). Same on
# every machine; carries no information about the dev network.
*	^10\.0\.2\.2$
# TURN deny-list ranges in hub/hub.mjs (audit b2). IETF-reserved
# ranges, identical on every network; not the dev LAN. Each range is
# written start-end, so both endpoint addresses need an entry.
hub/hub.mjs	^10\.0\.0\.0$
hub/hub.mjs	^10\.255\.255\.255$
hub/hub.mjs	^172\.16\.0\.0$
hub/hub.mjs	^172\.31\.255\.255$
hub/hub.mjs	^192\.168\.0\.0$
hub/hub.mjs	^192\.168\.255\.255$
# GitHub SSH remote user@host. Public service endpoint, not a personal
# email; appears in origin-URL handling.
*	^git@github\.com$
# Reserved example domain in the contribution template (audit c5).
*	^.+@example\.org$
# Upstream maintainer contact in lockfiles, not the user (audit c4).
*package-lock.json	^i@izs\.me$
# Reserved test domain; seed fixtures are fake by construction (audit b9).
*	^.+@test\.local$
# The allow-list itself names the waflurgiooh hostname in its entries and comments; exempt its own mentions so the file does not trip the scan.
ci/privacy-allowlist	^waflurgiooh$
# DCO sign-off identity (M18, 2026-11-21): every commit message
# carries "Signed-off-by: Crud <crudobi@proton.me>" — the public git
# identity, already in every commit trailer in the public history.
# The message scan would otherwise fail on every commit. Any OTHER
# address in a message still fails the scan.
*	^crudobi@proton\.me$
